    <!-- Guides (v1.7.7 Redesigned) -->
    <string name="tut_joy_t1">Connection Modes</string>
    <string name="tut_joy_d1">Choose your hardware: External pad, Pro Serial, or Network. System uses "Hardware Fingerprinting" to remember your setup.</string>
    <string name="tut_joy_t2">Setup Wizard</string>
    <string name="tut_joy_d2">[Recommended] Follow the wizard to auto-detect Mode 1~4 and map all channels instantly.</string>
    <string name="tut_joy_t3">Auto Binding</string>
    <string name="tut_joy_d3">For manual setup, click "Auto" next to an axis then move your remote. The system captures it in real-time.</string>
    <string name="tut_joy_t4">Polarity Invert</string>
    <string name="tut_joy_d4">If the drone moves opposite to your stick (e.g., pushes down instead of up), click the switch here to invert.</string>
    <string name="tut_joy_t5">Control Modes</string>
    <string name="tut_joy_d5">Switch between Mode 2 (USA) or Mode 1 (Japan). This changes the stick logic immediately.</string>
    <string name="tut_joy_t6">Joystick Calibration</string>
    <string name="tut_joy_d6">Recalibrate physical center points and limits to eliminate drift and ensure travel accuracy.</string>
    <string name="tut_joy_t7">AUX Mapping</string>
    <string name="tut_joy_d7">Bind motor arming, views, or gimbal tilt to physical switches on your remote controller.</string>
    <string name="tut_joy_t8">Sensitivity &amp; Rates</string>
    <string name="tut_joy_d8">Finally, adjust Rate and Expo in the right panel to customize your professional flight feel.</string>

    <string name="tut_clim_t1">Wind Level Control</string>
    <string name="tut_clim_d1">Set base wind speed. High levels increase drift and downwash. Level 1 is recommended for starters.</string>
    <string name="tut_clim_t2">360 Real-time Direction</string>
    <string name="tut_clim_d2">Select via 3x3 grid or Random (🎲). Watch the HUD compass: the arrow shows actual physics flow in real-time.</string>
    <string name="tut_clim_t3">Turbulence (Stochastic Pulse)</string>
    <string name="tut_clim_d3">No more predictable waves! This slider controls the frequency and intensity of random atmospheric pulses.</string>
    <string name="tut_clim_t4">Vertical Draft</string>
    <string name="tut_clim_d4">Enables "Downwash Dominance" simulation. Sudden drops in altitude will force active throttle compensation.</string>
    <string name="tut_clim_t5">Advanced Physics (Exp)</string>
    <string name="tut_clim_d5">Hardcore mode: Ground effect vanishing above 0.7m and lift loss during large-angle corrections.</string>
    <string name="tut_clim_t6">Visuals &amp; Mood</string>
    <string name="tut_clim_d6">Adjust sun position and weather presets. These affect visual cues only, not flight physics.</string>
    <string name="tut_clim_t7">Weather &amp; Cloud Control</string>
    <string name="tut_clim_d7">Switch between weather presets (e.g., Cumulus, Stratus). Once a cloudy mode is active, fine-tune the density for more challenging visual conditions.</string>
    <string name="tut_clim_t8">Distant Mountains</string>
    <string name="tut_clim_d8">Toggle the visibility of distant mountain ranges. Mountains provide essential depth perception and a more immersive scale.</string>

